  "title": "Web: small flow-state fixes (capture, PDF export, create, settings, versions, cookbook)",
  "description": "CapturePage.tsx handleMessage (25-57) doesn't check the status is 'waiting', so a second 'html' message starts a second capture. \
PdfExportModal.tsx: Cancel is disabled while generating but Escape/backdrop close isn't; generation continues and calls props.onClose()/doc.save afterwards (440-441). \
CreateRecipePage.tsx: three flows each with their own loading/error flags (15-58); scraping resets only on error (113); startingText + textStarted is a two-boolean encoding; toggleBookmarklet (60-75) can mint twice if toggled quickly. \
SettingsPage.tsx: errorMessage and uploadError live outside the status/uploadState unions (18-31); the name-status poll keeps its failure count in a closure (89-102). \
VersionHistoryPanel.tsx loads only when versions().length === 0 (66), so it doesn't refresh after a revert or accepted AI edit while mounted; RecipeVersioningSection.tsx:74-78 derives the compare modal's isOpen from three signals. \
Cookbook: selectAllStatus uses the string 'Loading…' as a state flag (useCookbookBulkSelection.ts:33, 105); error/notice are shared between list loads (which clear them, recipeRequests.ts:65-66) and bulk-op results. \
Found in the 2026-11-07 implicit-state-machine audit; line numbers are as of e94669d4ca, so re-check each point before fixing.",
